{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 3, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 5872821509810173328, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 626, "mtime": 1791872311.4319727, "sha256": "e037704445104969534cb2c5451176461fa1bb7685d5b833bebb7867d9a53f80"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 431, "mtime": 1791872314.975943, "sha256": "f6ea81ddfe36838de3b7e67ff2bdf2bacaec815ef025a21a408f30e1e6c5fa37"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/transcripts/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/20/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/cells/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/20/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Adding a regression test, then running it with the existing tests.\nFixed: `round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** in binary, the float `2.675` is stored as `2.67499999999999982\u2026`, so `round(x, 2)` correctly rounds it down. `round()` also uses banker's rounding (`round(0.125, 2) == 0.12`), which breaks the \"half up\" promise in the docstring.\n\n**Fix** (`pricing/money.py`): convert the float to `Decimal` via `repr(x)`, which gives the shortest form that maps back to the same float (`\"2.675\"`). Then round with `quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), ROUND_HALF_UP)`. It still returns a `float`, so callers (`add_vat`) get the same type as before.\n\n**Verification:** pytest isn't installed here, so I didn't run the test suite. I ran a direct call instead:\n- `round_money`: 2.675\u21922.68, 1.005\u21921.01, 0.125\u21920.13, 2.674\u21922.67, -2.675\u2192-2.68, 3\u21923.0\n- `add_vat(10)`\u219212.0, and `split(10.00, 3)` still gives `[3.34, 3.33, 3.33]`\n\nI added `tests/test_round_money.py` with those cases. It hasn't run under pytest yet.\n\n**Remaining issue:** `add_vat` multiplies floats before rounding, so new float error can creep in at that step. `add_vat(2.2375)` should be 2.685 \u2192 2.69, but the product is `2.6849999999999996`, so it returns `2.68`. Fixing it means doing the multiplication in `Decimal` inside `add_vat`. I left that alone because it's beyond what you asked; say if you want it.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 9, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 249686, "requests_cache_write": 8378, "requests_cost_usd": 0.14124720000000002, "requests_count": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 2467, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-